        -:  814:
        -:  815:These each coerce the given SV to UV and return it.  The returned value in many
        -:  816:circumstances will get stored in C<sv>'s UV slot, but not in all cases.  (Use
        -:  817:C<L</sv_setuv>> to make sure it does).
        -:  818:
        -:  819:As of 5.37.1, all are guaranteed to evaluate C<sv> only once.
        -:  820:
        -:  821:C<SvUVx> is now identical to C<SvUV>, but prior to 5.37.1, it was the only form
        -:  822:guaranteed to evaluate C<sv> only once.
        -:  823:
        -:  824:=cut
        -:  825:*/
